{"ts":"2026-07-17T09:33:14.995Z","type":"theory-option-declared","theory":"theory-20260717-live-claim-tenure-binding","scope":"frontier","frontier":"local-leadership-tenure-bound-safety-evidence-main","status":"active","layer":"ownership","mechanism":"The content-based preference cannot distinguish a row naming this node because its current live raft tenure seeded it from a fossil of an old tenure (equal-version post-teardown CDC replay), because it consults row content instead of the live localCanonicalLeaderObservation claim the seed maintains (with demoted/superseded flags). Binding the preference to the live claim - partition, node, raft term, and the causal version it was minted against, revalidated after every authoritative-read await - kills the old-tenure replay structurally, leaves only the irreducible not-yet-noticed-demotion window (floor-bounded), and retires content-based trust from the safety path","owner":"partition service metadata delivery (claim exposure with term and mint version) and priority-publication safety rows (claim-bound preference); floors, interlock, and seed lifecycle byte-unchanged per the sealed constraints","boundary":null,"callerRole":null,"missingTransition":null,"ownedFixPath":null,"tailConsumers":[],"intervention":"Expose a live getLocalCanonicalLeaderClaim from the partition service (term recorded at seed time), route it to the safety read via the repository, replace the content-based node-ID check with the claim-bound check revalidated post-await, and prove: replay-window discriminator red on content-based and green tenure-bound, in-flight demotion still fenced, third-party claims still defer, plus the TLA extension with the content-based mutant violating successor preference","expectedMovement":"The replay-window regression flips green under tenure-binding while all existing regressions hold; the quest scenario (guard-test runner) reaches 3 consecutive PASS","negativeResultMeans":"If the raft term is not available at seed time or the claim cannot be routed to the safety read without a second authority, the exposure design is wrong and the preference must instead be retired entirely until a safe conduit exists","discriminator":"Guard suite: replayed old-tenure self-naming row with no live claim must not be preferred; live claim demoted during the await must not be preferred; live current claim must be preferred; third-party rows defer; existing merge and TOCTOU regressions unchanged","modelGuidance":{"applies":true,"reasons":["owner-boundary language","model-contract language","handoff or lifecycle language"],"command":"npm run model:contracts","discriminator":"npm run model:contracts","modelRef":"model:architecture/contracts/core-system-logic.md","reportPattern":"test-output/reports/*.model.report.json","instruction":"Use this gate as the Quest theory discriminator for architecture, owner-boundary, core-system, lifecycle, or model-contract theories. At the model rung, pass the modelRef unless a finding explains why the architecture model is not applicable."},"promotionRule":"Promote when the guard suite is green with red-on-revert on the claim-binding, the TLA mutant/fixed pair meets expectations, adjacent safety suites hold, and an independent verifier approves the exposure as not constituting a second leadership authority","rejectionRule":"Reject if claim exposure weakens the single-authority contract (diagnostics becoming readiness authority) or any floor must change","evidence":"solve/changes/dt-prove/dt-local-leader-seed-safety-merge.test.js-2026-07-17T09-26-13-868Z.json","card":null}
