placement, connectivity, and concurrent-operation floors, the ledger interlock, and the seed lifecycle (demotion clear, demoted-replay re-null, superseded flags) remain byte-unchanged; tenure-binding only strengthens which local claim the preference may consult."},{"id":"replay-window-discriminator","statement":"A deterministic regression must reproduce the equal-version post-teardown CDC replay window red on the content-based preference (a replayed old-tenure self-naming row is preferred) and green under tenure-binding, alongside the existing in-flight-demotion and third-party-claim regressions; the irreducible not-yet-noticed-demotion window must be documented as out of scope with its floor bound."},{"id":"model-extension","statement":"Extend the local-leader-row-visibility or a focused new TLA model with an in-flight safety read holding captured cache evidence, a demotion/successor transition during the read, and an old-tenure replay: the content-based mutant must violate the successor-preference invariant while the tenure-bound spec holds it."}],"frontierIds":["local-leadership-tenure-bound-safety-evidence-main"]}}
